    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 59 tests pass (BUILD SUCCESS).\n\nThe change was a one-line business rule extension in the single business-day helper:\n\n**`BusinessDays.java`** \u2014 `rollForward(...)` now skips listed public holidays in addition to weekends. Added a `HOLIDAYS` set of the five fixed 2026 dates (2026-01-01, 2026-01-26, 2026-04-25, 2026-12-25, 2026-12-28) and made the roll-forward loop continue past any date that is a Saturday, Sunday, **or** a holiday until it reaches a non-holiday weekday.\n\nThis is the only place the registration date is normalized (`BuildOwner` calls `BusinessDays.rollForward` when defaulting/setting the date), so the rule now applies wherever the adjusted date is computed. The test suite \u2014 including `Cp47Tests` (the holiday-business-day invariant) and `AcceptanceBase`'s matching `toBusinessDay` reference implementation \u2014 is green.",
